From 89ff3d3461456a6b451aa0c370f00100685c1d1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Casey Connolly <casey.connolly@linaro.org>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 15:34:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 019/113] drm/panel: add LG SW43402 panel driver

Adds a DRM panel driver for the LG SW43402, a 1440x2880 DSI command
mode panel with DSC used on the Google Pixel 2 XL (taimen). Generated
with linux-mdss-dsi-panel-driver-generator from the vendor devicetree
and then adapted for runtime brightness updates while composing.

Runtime brightness needs two things:

 1. Strict DPU-kickoff vs DCS-DMA mutual exclusion in the DSI host
    (msm.cmd_frame_serialize): without it, a runtime write during
    composition corrupts the DSC stream (full-screen noise banded at
    slice boundaries, and a bad HS misframe can make the DDIC execute
    a phantom command and go dark) until a full panel re-init. Simple
    "wait for frame done" polling is not sufficient.

 2. Register 0x53 has to stay 0x00 (see lg_panel_enable()): with
    BCTRL set, a 0x51 brightness write latches but is never applied.

The display-on DCS (0x29) is deferred by ~5 frames after enable():
sending it inline flashes the DDIC's stale GRAM contents on every
unblank, since enable() runs before the first frame is written. The
delay lets real frames land in GRAM while the panel is still dark;
it is exposed as display_on_delay_ms since the right value is a
function of how fast the compositor gets a first frame out, which
varies by userspace stack.

Signed-off-by: Casey Connolly <casey.connolly@linaro.org>
Co-developed-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Kconfig            |  11 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/Makefile           |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c | 543 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 555 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-lg-sw43402.c

